  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lalit vs State Of U.P. on 6 July, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 82 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 17755 of 2020 Applicant :- Lalit Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Sunil Kumar Tripathi,Santosh Kukmar Tiwari Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "The instant bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicant, Lalit, with a prayer to release him on bail in Case Crime No. 138 of 2020, under Sections 147, 149, 272, 273, 307 IPC and 60 Excise Act, Police Station Kithore, District- Meerut, during pendency of trial. Submission is that implication of applicant is under Section 307 IPC. Intention of the applicant was only to evade arrest by the police and he fired only to frighten the police. It has been submitted that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 07.4.2020. Learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant.",
    "arguments": "Having considered the material on record, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Having considered the material on record, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1."
